(Y.2.1   Codec approach and specification) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.00 365.08 Tm
(In this approach, a codec is used to convert the digital input/output bit-stream of the system simulator to the) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.00 352.68 Tm
(equivalent analogue values. With this approach a system simulator simulating the radio link to the terminal under) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.00 340.28 Tm
(controlled and error-free conditions is required, unless otherwise specified for the respective test. The system) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.00 327.88 Tm
(simulator has to be equipped with a high-quality codec with characteristics as close as possible to ideal.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.00 306.48 Tm
(Definition of 0\240dBr point:) Tj
1 0 0 1 86.20 285.08 Tm
(D/A converter -    a Digital Test Sequence \(DTS\) representing the codec equivalent of an analogue sinusoidal) Tj
1 0 0 1 157.10 272.68 Tm
(signal with an RMS value of 3,14\240dB below the maximum full-load capacity of the codec shall) Tj
1 0 0 1 157.10 260.28 Tm
(generate 0 dBm across a 600\240ohm load;) Tj
1 0 0 1 86.20 238.88 Tm
(A/D converter -    a 0\240dBm signal generated from a 600\240ohm source shall give the digital test sequence \(DTS\)) Tj
1 0 0 1 157.10 226.48 Tm
(representing the codec equivalent of an analogue sinusoidal signal with an RMS value of) Tj
1 0 0 1 157.10 214.08 Tm
(3,14\240dB below the maximum full-load capacity of the codec.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.00 192.68 Tm
/F10 10.0 Tf
(Channel-based telephony testing) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.00 171.28 Tm
/F9 10.0 Tf
(For testing of a LTE, 5G NR or WLAN terminal supporting multi-channel telephony, the system simulator shall use) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.00 158.88 Tm
(the IVAS speech codec [configuration TBD \214].) Tj
1 0 0 1 86.20 137.48 Tm
1.000 0.000 0.000 rg
(Editor\221s Note:      IVAS may not yet be available for the specification of test configurations. During this period) Tj
1 0 0 1 128.75 125.08 Tm
(linear PCM coding of the signals should be assumed to derive appropriate requirements that may need) Tj
